# Change Log

All notable changes to gempa software manger(GSM) will be documented in this file.

## 2026.301 1.8.1

### Added

-   `gsm print nagios licenses` nagios check to verify the validity of the licenses

### Changed

-   Improved gsm info output
-   `license_info_days = 0` switches the notice about a license that ends soon
    off (`update`, `print nagios licenses`); an expired license is still reported

### Fixed

-   `gsm show <package>` the output is better on smaller terminals

## 2026.300 1.8.0

### Added

-   More options to shell-completion
-   More detailed log information. Use --debug command line switch for more verbose
    logging information.
-   Show history of a package

    ```
    gsm show history package
    ```

### Changed

-   Rework the terminal output
-   Configuration packages are updated if none of their files was edited;
    modified files are kept and the new version is written as `<file>.gsmnew`
-   User name and password are sent only to `base_url` and `db_url`
-   Report every Important entry newer than the installed version

### Fixed

-   Option `--downloadonly` when upgrading release
-   Licenses are fetched again if missing, expired or too old for the new
    version
-   In offline mode gsm is updated only if the new gsm package has been downloaded
-   Removing or updating `slabs-rum` and `slabs-usgs` failed after an
    installation with gsm 1.7
-   Interrupted copies and backups left half files behind
-   Broken sync cache after core.db could not be unpacked
-   `gsm alias create` accepted a name with a line break
-   Migration 0.2 -> 0.3 turned `var/sync` into `var/var/sync` when running twice

## 2026.202 1.7.2

### Added

-   Option to run gsm setup non interactive

    ```
    gsm setup -y
    ```

-   Add '-f' to localinstall, force a package reinstall even if the
    package version is lower than the currently installed version.

### Fixed

-   Broken --showurls option
-   Restore feature revised and made more robust
-   Optional dependency handling

## 2026.177 1.7.1

### Fixed

-   Upgrade support for releases that do not have migration 0.3 applied

## 2026.173 1.7.0

### Important

-   The following error messages appear during the update and can be ignored:

    ```
    ./gsm: line 104: nge: command not found
    ./gsm: line 116: run_gsm: command not found
    ```

### Added

-   Option to print Nagios crontab entry and service
-   Linux Mint support
-   New Option --to (for do-release-upgrade and do-release-downgrade) that allows
    to select the target release directly
-   Show history (search the log file for a package to find relevant entries)

### Changed

-   Drop SeisComP3 support

## 2026.139 1.6.17

### Fixed

-   3rd-party library compatibility issue with timedinput

## 2026.054 1.6.16

### Important

-   Please run `gsm reinstall` after the update to complete the installation.

### Added

-   Some users have multiple SeisComP installations on the same
    system, each installation required a separate GSM installation.
    With this release we have introduced alias support in GSM which
    allows users to manage any number of installations using a single
    GSM instance. A new alias can be created as follows:

    ```
    gsm alias create <name>
    ```

-   Display download sizes of optional packages
-   If gsm is in your $PATH which is now checked during setup you can use tab completion.
    To do this, the file located at: share/shell-completion/gsm.bash must be
    included in $HOME/.bashrc
    This can be added to $HOME/.bashrc as follows (just an example):

    ```
    source "/home/xxx/install/gsm/share/shell-completion/gsm.bash"
    ```

### Changed

-   This is the last GSM release that still supports an upgrade
    from SeisComP3 to a new release. This feature will be removed in the next release.
-   Track core.db modification time in a extra file as some users
    had issues when the core.db file modification time has been
    modified, e.g., by Git.
-   The following directories and files have been moved as follows:

    ```
    gsm.conf --> etc/gsm.conf
    libs --> lib
    sync --> var/sync
    packages --> var/packages
    venv --> var/venv
    log --> var/log
    CHANGELOG --> share/doc/gsm/CHANGELOG
    ```

### Fixed

-   Problems with release up- or downgrade when packages are not available for
    the target release.

